# Deep links for the client routes in src/main.jsx. Deliberately NOT a `/*`
# catch-all: that matched /assets/* too, so an asset request that missed at an
# edge during a deploy came back as 200 text/html instead of a 404 — and the
# /assets/* rule in _headers then marked that wrong answer `immutable` for a
# year. Edge and browser cached an HTML document under a .css/.js URL, and
# whoever hit that node got an unstyled page (stylesheet refused) or a blank
# one (script refused) until the cache expired.
#
# With no rule matching /assets/*, a miss is a real 404, which no browser will
# apply as a stylesheet or cache as a valid asset. Unknown paths now get the
# Pages 404 rather than being bounced to "/" by the router.
/industries/*  /index.html  200
